Exercise 1 - Test Case Design

Happy Path

TC-01: Send Gift Successfully with Valid Data
Category: Happy Path
Priority: P0
Preconditions:
User is authenticated with a valid Sanctum token.
User has joined room 12345.
User wallet balance is 10,000 coins.
Gift price is 500 coins.
Room audience size is at least 5 users.
Steps:
Send POST request to /api/gifts/send.
Use valid room_id, gift_id, quantity=10, winners_count=5, and a valid UUID v4 idempotency key.
Expected Result:
Response status code is 200.
Response contains transaction_id.
coins_charged equals expected amount.
winners array contains 5 unique users.
remaining_balance is correctly calculated.
Wallet balance is deducted in database.
gift.sent event is broadcast successfully.
Why it matters:
Verifies the complete successful transaction flow.

TC-02: Send Gift Using Minimum Allowed Values
Category: Happy Path
Priority: P1
Preconditions:
User is authenticated.
User has sufficient balance.
Room contains at least one viewer.
Steps:
Send request with quantity=1.
Set winners_count=1.
Expected Result:
Status code 200.
Transaction created successfully.
One winner is selected.
Correct coin deduction occurs.
Why it matters:
Validates lower boundary values.

TC-03: Wallet Balance Exactly Equals Required Cost
Category: Happy Path
Priority: P0
Preconditions:
Wallet balance equals quantity × gift.coin_price exactly.
Steps:
Submit valid gift request.
Expected Result:
Request succeeds.
Remaining balance becomes 0.
Transaction recorded successfully.
Why it matters:
Verifies balance boundary handling.
Validation

